&lt;h3 id="hugo-shortcodes"&gt;Hugo Shortcodes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adding support to a new HTML DOM in your Hugo site is possible using Hugo &lt;a href="https://gohugo.io/content-management/shortcodes/"&gt;shortcodes&lt;/a&gt;.
Which is a way to add custom HTML elements to your website like image, video, and HTML canvas.
The shortcode is a HTML template invoked within markup, accepting any number of arguments.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Hugo: Adding TeX Support</title><link>https://mizerc.github.io/posts/hugo/tex-support/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mizerc.github.io/posts/hugo/tex-support/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://katex.org/"&gt;KaTeX&lt;/a&gt; library allow you to enable TeX support to your hugo website.
The library supports all major browsers.
TeX syntax allows us to write mathematical formulas and scientific symbols easily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$$
\int_a^b f(x) dx
$$&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="installing"&gt;Installing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To install, we just need to import the library files from some CDN to our Hugo website.
One way to do this is using the &lt;strong&gt;Hugo partials&lt;/strong&gt; which allow us to import small HTML context.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Hugo: helloworld</title><link>https://mizerc.github.io/posts/hugo/hugo/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mizerc.github.io/posts/hugo/hugo/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hugo is a static site generator developed in Go.
